  "doc": "benefits_guide.pdf",
  "title": "2027 Benefits Guide",
  "synthetic": true,
  "pages": [
    [
      {
        "h": "Front Range Civic Software, Inc.<br/>2027 Benefits Guide"
      },
      {
        "p": "For new hires starting January 2027 and for open enrollment in November 2027."
      },
      {
        "h": "Contents"
      },
      {
        "p": "2 Eligibility and enrollment<br/>3 Medical plans at a glance<br/>4 Medical plan costs<br/>5 Health Savings Account (HSA)<br/>6 FSA, dental and vision<br/>7 401(k) retirement plan<br/>8 Employee Stock Purchase Plan (ESPP)<br/>9 Life and disability insurance<br/>10 Contacts and glossary"
      }
    ],
    [
      {
        "h": "Eligibility and enrollment"
      },
      {
        "p": "Full-time employees scheduled for 30 or more hours a week are eligible on their first day. You may cover your spouse or domestic partner and your children to age 26."
      },
      {
        "p": "New hires have 30 days from their start date to enroll. For the January 4, 2027 new-hire cohort, the enrollment deadline is February 3, 2027. Coverage is retroactive to your start date."
      },
      {
        "p": "If you miss the deadline, you can change your elections only at open enrollment each November, or within 30 days of a qualifying life event such as marriage, birth or adoption, or losing other coverage."
      }
    ],
    [
      {
        "h": "Medical plans at a glance"
      },
      {
        "p": "We offer three medical plans through the same national carrier network. All three cover the same services, and in-network preventive care is free on every plan."
      },
      {
        "p": "PPO 750: the highest paycheck cost and the lowest deductible. Copays for office visits start right away."
      },
      {
        "p": "PPO 1500: a middle option, with a lower paycheck cost and a higher deductible."
      },
      {
        "p": "HDHP with HSA: the lowest paycheck cost and the highest deductible. It is the only plan that lets you open a Health Savings Account, and the company adds money to it (see page 5)."
      }
    ],
    [
      {
        "h": "Medical plan costs"
      },
      {
        "p": "Premiums below are your share, taken from each of your 26 biweekly paychecks before taxes."
      },
      {
        "table": [
          [
            "Biweekly employee cost",
            "PPO 750",
            "PPO 1500",
            "HDHP with HSA"
          ],
          [
