            "10%"
          ]
        ]
      },
      {
        "p": "Family deductibles and out-of-pocket maximums apply to every tier that covers a dependent."
      }
    ],
    [
      {
        "h": "Health Savings Account (HSA)"
      },
      {
        "p": "If you enroll in the HDHP with HSA, the company contributes to your HSA each year: $500 per year for employee-only coverage, or $1,000 per year for any tier that covers a dependent. The company contribution is deposited in equal amounts each paycheck."
      },
      {
        "p": "You can add your own pre-tax money up to the annual IRS limit, which includes the company's contribution. See irs.gov for the current year's limit."
      },
      {
        "p": "An HSA has three tax benefits: money goes in before tax, grows without tax, and comes out without tax for qualified medical expenses. The account is yours to keep if you leave the company."
      }
    ],
    [
      {
        "h": "Flexible Spending Account (FSA)"
      },
      {
        "p": "PPO members can set aside pre-tax money in a health care FSA, up to the annual IRS limit. Unused FSA money above the carryover amount is lost at the end of the plan year. You cannot have a health care FSA and an HSA at the same time."
      },
      {
        "h": "Dental and vision"
      },
      {
        "p": "Dental: $50 deductible, preventive cleanings covered at 100%, $1,500 annual maximum. Biweekly cost: $4.50 employee only, $12.00 family."
      },
      {
        "p": "Vision: $10 exam copay, $150 frame allowance every 24 months. Biweekly cost: $1.80 employee only, $4.75 family."
      }
    ],
    [
      {
        "h": "401(k) retirement plan"
      },
      {
        "p": "You can save from 1% to 75% of your eligible pay in the 401(k), as traditional pre-tax, Roth after-tax, or both, up to the annual IRS limit."
      },
      {
        "p": "Company match: the company contributes 50 cents for every dollar you contribute, on the first 6% of your eligible pay. To receive the full match, which equals 3% of your pay, you must contribute at least 6%."
      },
      {
        "p": "Automatic enrollment: new hires are enrolled at 3% of pay unless they choose a different rate within 30 days."
      },
      {
        "p": "Vesting: your own contributions are always 100% yours. Company match contributions vest 20% per year of service and are fully vested after 5 years."
      }
    ],
    [
      {
        "h": "Employee Stock Purchase Plan (ESPP)"
      },
      {
        "p": "The ESPP lets you buy company stock at a 15% discount through payroll deductions. You may contribute 1% to 15% of your eligible pay, after taxes."
      },
      {
        "p": "The plan has six-month offering periods, starting January 1 and July 1. Shares are bought on the last trading day of each period."
      },
      {
        "p": "The plan includes a lookback: the purchase price is 85% of the lower of the stock price on the first day or the last day of the offering period."
      },
      {
        "p": "Holding period: shares bought through the ESPP cannot be sold for 180 days after the purchase date."
      },
      {
        "p": "You cannot buy more than $25,000 of stock, valued at the start of each offering period, in any calendar year, or more than 750 shares in any one offering period."
      }
    ],
    [
      {
        "h": "Life and disability insurance"
      },
      {
        "p": "Basic life insurance of one times your annual salary is provided at no cost. You may buy supplemental life coverage for yourself, your spouse, and your children."
      },
      {
        "p": "Short-term disability pays 60% of your salary for up to 12 weeks, after a 7-day waiting period, at no cost to you. Long-term disability pays 60% of your salary, up to $10,000 a month, after 90 days."
      }
    ],
    [
      {
        "h": "Contacts"
      },
      {
        "p": "Benefits questions: People Operations, benefits@frontrange-civic.example"
      },
      {
        "h": "Glossary"
      },
      {
        "p": "Premium: what you pay each paycheck to have the plan.<br/>Deductible: what you pay for care each year before the plan starts paying.<br/>Out-of-pocket maximum: the most you pay for covered care in a year.<br/>Coinsurance: your share of a bill after the deductible.<br/>Vesting: when company contributions become yours to keep."
      },
      {
        "p": "This guide is a summary. If it differs from the official plan documents, the plan documents govern. Confirm your choices with People Operations or a licensed advisor."
      }
    ]
  ],
